    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first creates a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into windows while preserving tokens.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder maps the low-resolution image into the dense feature field. The field is the carrier that holds spatial information for the method. Window partitioning turns that field into tokens for the thought process. The equation keeps every token by applying the window operation to the feature field, not to a compact state.",
      "evidence": [
